{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "def is_not_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return True if n is not a prime number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return True\n    if n == 2:\n        return False\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return True\n    limit = int(n**0.5) + 1\n    for i in range(3, limit, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return True\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "def find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum number of rotations (greater than 0) required to get the same string.\n    Uses the KMP prefix function (LPS array) to determine the string's smallest period.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # Compute the LPS (Longest Proper Prefix which is also Suffix) array for the string s.\n    lps = [0] * n\n    length = 0  # Length of the previous longest prefix suffix\n    i = 1\n    while i < n:\n        if s[i] == s[length]:\n            length += 1\n            lps[i] = length\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            if length != 0:\n                length = lps[length - 1]\n            else:\n                lps[i] = 0\n                i += 1\n    \n    # The length of the smallest repeating unit (period) is n - lps[n-1].\n    # If the string length 'n' is perfectly divisible by this period,\n    # then this period is the minimum number of rotations. Otherwise, 'n' rotations are needed.\n    period = n - lps[n - 1]\n    \n    if n % period == 0:\n        return period\n    else:\n        return n"}
