{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "class StringManipulator:\n    def remove_occurrence(self, input: str, char: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Removes first and last occurrence of char from input.\n        Handles various edge cases and multiple occurrences.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not input or len(char) != 1:\n            return input\n\n        first = input.find(char)\n        last = input.rfind(char)\n\n        # No occurrences\n        if first == -1:\n            return input\n\n        # Fewer than two occurrences: remove all\n        if first == last:\n            return input.replace(char, '')\n\n        # Remove first and last by slicing\n        return input[:first] + input[first + 1:last] + input[last + 1:]\n\n_manipulator = StringManipulator()\n\ndef remove_Occ(input: str, char: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Public API that removes first and last occurrence of char.\n    Delegates to StringManipulator.remove_occurrence.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _manipulator.remove_occurrence(input, char)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/14", "solution": "class TriangularPrism:\n    \"\"\"Represents a triangular prism with given dimensions.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, base: int, height: int, length: int):\n        self.base = base\n        self.height = height\n        self.length = length\n\n    def volume(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the volume of the triangular prism.\"\"\"\n        return (self.base * self.height // 2) * self.length\n\ndef find_Volume(base: int, height: int, length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the volume of a triangular prism.\"\"\"\n    prism = TriangularPrism(base, height, length)\n    return prism.volume()"}
