{"task_id": "Mbpp/20", "solution": "def is_woodall(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is a Woodall number.\n    A Woodall number is of the form n * 2^n - 1 for some positive integer n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        woodall_candidate = k * (2**k) - 1\n        if woodall_candidate == num:\n            return True\n        elif woodall_candidate > num:\n            return False\n        k += 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "def check(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    The reverse of a number is obtained by reversing its decimal digits, preserving the sign.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _reverse_int_helper(num):\n        if num == 0:\n            return 0\n        \n        sign = -1 if num < 0 else 1\n        abs_num_str = str(abs(num))\n        reversed_abs_str = abs_num_str[::-1]\n        \n        return sign * int(reversed_abs_str)\n\n    class _Number:\n        def __init__(self, value, reversed_value):\n            self.value = value\n            self.reverse = reversed_value\n\n        def is_one_less_than_twice_reverse(self):\n            return self.value == (2 * self.reverse) - 1\n\n    reversed_n = _reverse_int_helper(n)\n    number_obj = _Number(n, reversed_n)\n    return number_obj.is_one_less_than_twice_reverse()"}
