{"task_id": "Mbpp/65", "solution": "def recursive_list_sum(nested_list: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Recursively sums all integer elements in a nested list.\n\n    Args:\n        nested_list (list): A list that may contain integers or other lists.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: Sum of all integer elements.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If an element is not an int or list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(nested_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list\")\n\n    total = 0\n    for element in nested_list:\n        if isinstance(element, int):\n            total += element\n        elif isinstance(element, list):\n            total += recursive_list_sum(element)\n        else:\n            raise TypeError(\"List elements must be int or list\")\n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the nth Bell number, which represents the number of partitions of a set with n elements.\n    It uses dynamic programming to calculate Stirling numbers of the second kind.\n    \"\"\"\n    stirling = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case for Stirling numbers of the second kind: S(0, 0) = 1\n    stirling[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the table for Stirling numbers S(i, j)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Recurrence relation: S(i, j) = S(i-1, j-1) + j * S(i-1, j)\n            stirling[i][j] = stirling[i-1][j-1] + j * stirling[i-1][j]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the sum of S(n, k) for k from 0 to n\n    bell_n = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        bell_n += stirling[n][k]\n\n    return bell_n"}
