{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_str: str, rotation_count: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Count how many cyclic left rotations of a binary string produce an odd integer.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    binary_str : str\n        Binary string composed of '0' and '1'.\n    rotation_count : int\n        Number of rotations to evaluate (non\u2011negative).\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    int\n        The number of rotations that result in an odd integer.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    ValueError\n        If binary_str contains non\u2011binary characters or rotation_count is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not all(c in '01' for c in binary_str):\n        raise ValueError(\"binary_str must contain only '0' and '1'\")\n    if rotation_count < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"rotation_count must be non\u2011negative\")\n\n    count = 0\n    length = len(binary_str)\n    for i in range(rotation_count):\n        # Perform a cyclic left rotation of the string\n        rotated = binary_str[i:] + binary_str[:i]\n        # Convert the rotated binary string to an integer and check if it's odd\n        if int(rotated, 2) & 1:\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
