{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "solution": "def search(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the element that appears only once in a sorted array where all other elements appear twice.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n\n        # Check if mid is part of a pair\n        # If mid is even, check with mid+1\n        # If mid is odd, check with mid-1\n        if mid % 2 == 0:  # mid is an even index\n            if array[mid] == array[mid + 1]:\n                # Pair found, unique element is to the right\n                low = mid + 2\n            else:\n                # Unique element is at mid or to its left\n                high = mid\n        else:  # mid is an odd index\n            if array[mid] == array[mid - 1]:\n                # Pair found, unique element is to the right\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                # Unique element is at mid or to its left\n                high = mid\n\n    # When low == high, we have found the single element\n    return array[low]"}
