{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(input_list):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements in ascending order using pancake sort, returning a new sorted list.\"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a shallow copy to ensure immutability as per FR1 and BR4.\n    arr = list(input_list)\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Iterate from the last element down to the second (index 1)\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find index of the maximum element in the current_size sublist\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, current_size):\n            if arr[i] > arr[max_idx]:\n                max_idx = i\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at the end of the current sublist\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            # Flip the sublist from 0 to max_idx to bring the maximum element to the beginning\n            arr[:max_idx + 1] = arr[:max_idx + 1][::-1]\n\n            # Flip the sublist from 0 to current_size - 1 to move the maximum element to its final sorted position\n            arr[:current_size] = arr[:current_size][::-1]\n\n    return arr"}
