{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "def find_even_pair(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of pairs of integers in a list that xor to an even number.\n    A pair (a, b) has an even XOR if both a and b are even, or both are odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    count_odd = 0\n    count_even = 0\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            count_even += 1\n        else:\n            count_odd += 1\n\n    # Number of pairs of odd numbers: nC2 = n * (n - 1) / 2\n    # Number of pairs of even numbers: mC2 = m * (m - 1) / 2\n    even_xor_pairs = (count_odd * (count_odd - 1) // 2) + \\\n                     (count_even * (count_even - 1) // 2)\n\n    return even_xor_pairs"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/165", "solution": "def count_char_position(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts characters whose 1-based string index matches their 1-based alphabetic position (case-insensitive).\n    Non-alphabetic characters are ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    s_lower = s.lower()\n    for i, char in enumerate(s_lower):\n        string_position = i + 1  # 1-based index for string position\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            alphabet_position = ord(char) - ord('a') + 1  # 1-based index for alphabet position\n            if string_position == alphabet_position:\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
