{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(arr, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    The majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    def find_first(arr, n, target):\n        low = 0\n        high = n - 1\n        first_occurrence = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                first_occurrence = mid\n                high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return first_occurrence\n\n    def find_last(arr, n, target):\n        low = 0\n        high = n - 1\n        last_occurrence = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                last_occurrence = mid\n                low = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return last_occurrence\n\n    first_idx = find_first(arr, n, element)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = find_last(arr, n, element)\n\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    return count > n / 2"}
