{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of set bits (1s) in the binary representation of a non-negative integer.\n    Uses Brian Kernighan's algorithm for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input number must be non-negative.\")\n\n    count = 0\n    while number > 0:\n        number &= (number - 1)  # Clear the least significant set bit\n        count += 1\n    return count"}
