{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "from typing import Tuple\n\nTupleOfPairs = Tuple[Tuple[int, int], ...]\n\ndef maximize_elements(\n    tuple1: TupleOfPairs,\n    tuple2: TupleOfPairs\n) -> TupleOfPairs:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a new tuple where each pair contains the element-wise maximum of the corresponding input pairs.\n    Raises ValueError if input tuples differ in length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n    return tuple(\n        (max(a[0], b[0]), max(a[1], b[1]))\n        for a, b in zip(tuple1, tuple2)\n    )"}
