{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(array, n, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the maximum contiguous sub\u2011array sum over the array repeated k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0 or k == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Kadane's algorithm for a single copy, and calculations for total, prefix, suffix sums\n    max_ending_here = max_so_far = array[0]\n    total_sum = array[0]\n    max_prefix = array[0]\n    current_prefix = array[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        # Kadane's algorithm for max subarray sum within a single array\n        max_ending_here = max(array[i], max_ending_here + array[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n\n        # Calculate total sum\n        total_sum += array[i]\n\n        # Calculate maximum prefix sum\n        current_prefix += array[i]\n        max_prefix = max(max_prefix, current_prefix)\n\n    # Calculate maximum suffix sum\n    max_suffix = array[-1]\n    current_suffix = array[-1]\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        current_suffix += array[i]\n        max_suffix = max(max_suffix, current_suffix)\n\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_so_far\n    else:\n        # If total sum is positive, it's beneficial to include (k-2) full copies\n        if total_sum > 0:\n            return max(max_so_far, max_suffix + max_prefix + (k - 2) * total_sum)\n        # If total sum is non-positive, it's never beneficial to include more than two copies\n        else:\n            return max(max_so_far, max_suffix + max_prefix)"}
