{"task_id": "Mbpp/290", "solution": "import collections\nfrom typing import List, Any, Tuple\n\ndef max_length(list_of_lists: List[List[Any]]) -> Tuple[int, List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the list of maximum length in a list of lists and returns its length and the list itself.\n    If multiple lists have the same maximum length, the first one encountered is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    max_len = -1\n    max_sublist = []\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        current_len = len(sublist)\n        if current_len > max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n            max_sublist = sublist\n\n    return (max_len, max_sublist)"}
