{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Optional\n\ndef max_Product(values: List[int]) -> Optional[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair of integers with the highest product from a given array.\n    This function processes the array in a single pass, tracking the two largest\n    and two smallest numbers to achieve linear time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(values) < 2:\n        return None\n\n    # Initialize variables to track the two largest and two smallest numbers found so far.\n    # Use float('-inf') and float('inf') to ensure any initial integer value will update them.\n    max1 = float('-inf')  # Largest number\n    max2 = float('-inf')  # Second largest number\n    min1 = float('inf')   # Smallest number\n    min2 = float('inf')   # Second smallest number\n\n    for n in values:\n        # Update the two largest numbers\n        if n > max1:\n            max2 = max1\n            max1 = n\n        elif n > max2:\n            max2 = n\n\n        # Update the two smallest numbers\n        if n < min1:\n            min2 = min1\n            min1 = n\n        elif n < min2:\n            min2 = n\n\n    # Calculate the products of the two largest and two smallest numbers.\n    # The highest product could come from two large positive numbers, or two small negative numbers.\n    product_of_two_largest = max1 * max2\n    product_of_two_smallest = min1 * min2\n\n    if product_of_two_largest >= product_of_two_smallest:\n        # Return the pair in ascending order (second largest, largest)\n        return (int(max2), int(max1))\n    else:\n        # Return the pair in ascending order (smallest, second smallest)\n        return (int(min1), int(min2))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/420", "solution": "def cube_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the cubes of the first n even natural numbers.\n    Assumes n is a non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        even_number = 2 * i\n        total_sum += even_number ** 3\n    return total_sum"}
