{"task_id": "Mbpp/432", "solution": "def median_trapezium(base1: float, base2: float, side: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median length of a trapezium given its two bases and a side.\n    The median is the arithmetic mean of the two bases.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(base1, (int, float)) or base1 <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"base1 must be a numeric value greater than zero.\")\n    if not isinstance(base2, (int, float)) or base2 <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"base2 must be a numeric value greater than zero.\")\n    if not isinstance(side, (int, float)) or side <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"side must be a numeric value greater than zero.\")\n\n    return (base1 + base2) / 2.0"}
