{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "import re\nfrom typing import Tuple\n\n# The regex pattern to find adverbs ending in 'ly'.\n# \\b ensures word boundaries. (\\w+?ly) captures the adverb itself.\n# re.IGNORECASE makes the match case-insensitive.\n_ADVERB_PATTERN = re.compile(r'\\b(\\w+?ly)\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> Tuple[int, int, str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the first adverb in the given sentence.\n\n    Returns (-1, -1, '') if no adverb is found, adhering to the constraint\n    of not raising exceptions for edge cases.\n    \"\"\"\n    match = _ADVERB_PATTERN.search(sentence)\n    if not match:\n        return -1, -1, ''\n    \n    adverb = match.group(1)\n    start = match.start(1)\n    end = match.end(1)\n    return start, end, adverb"}
