{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "from typing import Tuple, Union\n\nNumber = Union[int, float]\nInnerTuple = Tuple[Number, Number]\nOuterTuple = Tuple[InnerTuple, ...]\n\ndef index_multiplication(tuple1: OuterTuple, tuple2: OuterTuple) -> OuterTuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Perform index-wise multiplication of tuple elements in the given two tuples.\n    Each corresponding inner tuple has its elements multiplied together.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for inner1, inner2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        product_first = inner1[0] * inner2[0]\n        product_second = inner1[1] * inner2[1]\n        result.append((product_first, product_second))\n    return tuple(result)"}
