{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from index 0 to n.\n    P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2; for n>=3, P(n)=P(n-2)+P(n-3).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 3\n    if n == 1:\n        return 3\n    if n == 2:\n        return 5\n\n    # Initialize perrin sequence with P(0), P(1), P(2)\n    # and their sum\n    a, b, c = 3, 0, 2  # P(0), P(1), P(2)\n    current_sum = a + b + c\n\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        next_perrin = a + b  # P(n) = P(n-2) + P(n-3) where a is P(n-3) and b is P(n-2)\n        current_sum += next_perrin\n        a, b, c = b, c, next_perrin # Shift values: P(n-3) becomes P(n-2), P(n-2) becomes P(n-1), P(n-1) becomes P(n)\n\n    return current_sum"}
