{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def tuple_intersection(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the intersection of tuples between two lists, treating tuples as unordered sets of elements.\n    Converts tuples to frozensets for comparison and back to sorted tuples for the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    set1_normalized = {frozenset(t) for t in list1}\n    set2_normalized = {frozenset(t) for t in list2}\n\n    intersection_frozensets = set1_normalized.intersection(set2_normalized)\n\n    # Convert frozensets back to sorted tuples to ensure consistent output format\n    result_set = {tuple(sorted(f)) for f in intersection_frozensets}\n    return result_set"}
