{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "def count_Pairs(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of unordered pairs of distinct integers in a list.\n    Returns 0 if the list has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(lst)\n    if n < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    freq = {}\n    for num in lst:\n        freq[num] = freq.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    total_possible_pairs = n * (n - 1) // 2\n    pairs_with_equal_elements = 0\n    for count in freq.values():\n        pairs_with_equal_elements += count * (count - 1) // 2\n    \n    return total_possible_pairs - pairs_with_equal_elements"}
