{"task_id": "Mbpp/566", "solution": "class Number:\n    def __init__(self, value: int):\n        self.value = value\n\nclass DigitSumCalculator:\n    def sumDigits(self, n: Number) -> int:\n        num = n.value\n        if num < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n        \n        total_sum = 0\n        s_num = str(num) # Convert to string for easy digit access\n        for digit_char in s_num:\n            total_sum += int(digit_char)\n        return total_sum\n\ndef sum_digits(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the digits of a non-negative integer.\n    Orchestrates domain objects to perform the digit sum calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    number_obj = Number(n)\n    calculator = DigitSumCalculator()\n    return calculator.sumDigits(number_obj)"}
