{"task_id": "Mbpp/605", "solution": "def prime_num(value: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer is a prime number using an O(sqrt(n)) algorithm.\n    Handles negative numbers, 0, and 1 as non-prime.\n    \"\"\"\n    if value <= 1:\n        return False\n    if value == 2 or value == 3:\n        return True\n    if value % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    \n    # Check for divisors from 3 up to sqrt(value), only odd numbers\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= value:\n        if value % i == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 2\n            \n    return True"}
