{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of integers using the heap sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted list, leaving the original list unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(lst)\n    arr = list(lst)  # Create a copy to sort in-place and satisfy O(1) additional space beyond output.\n\n    # Helper function to maintain the max-heap property for a subtree rooted at i.\n    def heapify(arr_local, n_local, i_local):\n        largest = i_local  # Initialize largest as root\n        left = 2 * i_local + 1  # left child\n        right = 2 * i_local + 2  # right child\n\n        # See if left child of root exists and is greater than root\n        if left < n_local and arr_local[left] > arr_local[largest]:\n            largest = left\n\n        # See if right child of root exists and is greater than current largest\n        if right < n_local and arr_local[right] > arr_local[largest]:\n            largest = right\n\n        # Change root, if needed\n        if largest != i_local:\n            arr_local[i_local], arr_local[largest] = arr_local[largest], arr_local[i_local]  # swap\n            # Heapify the root.\n            heapify(arr_local, n_local, largest)\n\n    # Build a max-heap (rearrange array)\n    # The loop runs from the last non-leaf node down to the root.\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    # One by one extract elements from the heap\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]  # Move current root to end\n        heapify(arr, i, 0)  # Call heapify on the reduced heap\n\n    return arr"}
