{"task_id": "Mbpp/643", "solution": "import re\nfrom typing import Iterable\n\ndef text_match_wordz_middle(input: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns True if the input string contains the character 'z'\n    in the middle of any word (not at the start or end of the word).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Regular expression to split on non\u2011alphabetic characters\n    words: Iterable[str] = re.split(r'[^A-Za-z]+', input)\n    for word in words:\n        if len(word) < 3:\n            continue  # Cannot have a middle character\n        # Check each position except first and last\n        for i in range(1, len(word) - 1):\n            if word[i].lower() == 'z':\n                return True\n    return False"}
