{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum average cost of a path from the top-left to the bottom-right\n    of a square matrix, moving only right or down.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(matrix)\n\n    # dp[r][c] stores the maximum sum of costs to reach cell (r, c).\n    dp = [[0.0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Base case: The cost to reach the starting cell (0, 0) is its own value.\n    dp[0][0] = float(matrix[0][0])\n\n    # Fill the first row: can only come from the left.\n    for c in range(1, n):\n        dp[0][c] = dp[0][c - 1] + matrix[0][c]\n\n    # Fill the first column: can only come from above.\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        dp[r][0] = dp[r - 1][0] + matrix[r][0]\n\n    # Fill the rest of the dp table.\n    # To reach cell (r, c), one must come from (r-1, c) (moving down)\n    # or from (r, c-1) (moving right).\n    # We choose the path that yields the maximum sum.\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        for c in range(1, n):\n            dp[r][c] = max(dp[r - 1][c], dp[r][c - 1]) + matrix[r][c]\n\n    # The maximum total cost to reach the bottom-right cell is dp[n-1][n-1].\n    max_total_cost = dp[n - 1][n - 1]\n\n    # For any path from (0,0) to (n-1, n-1) moving only right or down,\n    # the number of cells visited is always 2*n - 1.\n    num_cells_in_path = 2 * n - 1\n\n    return max_total_cost / num_cells_in_path"}
