{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "import math\n\ndef find_min_diff(sequence, length):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum absolute difference between any two distinct elements in a sequence.\n\n    Ensures the sequence length is valid and sorts the sequence to find the minimum difference efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    if length < 2 or length != len(sequence):\n        raise ValueError(\"Sequence must contain at least two elements and length must match len(sequence).\")\n\n    sorted_sequence = sorted(list(sequence))\n    min_diff = math.inf\n\n    for i in range(1, length):\n        min_diff = min(min_diff, sorted_sequence[i] - sorted_sequence[i-1])\n\n    return min_diff"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "def find_nth_polite_number(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth polite number. A polite number is a positive integer that is not a power of two.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    i = 1\n    while True:\n        # Check if i is a power of two: (i > 0 and (i & (i - 1)) == 0)\n        # Since i starts from 1 and increments, i will always be > 0.\n        if (i & (i - 1)) == 0:  # i is a power of two\n            pass\n        else:  # i is not a power of two\n            count += 1\n            if count == n:\n                return i\n        i += 1"}
