{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "from collections import defaultdict\n\ndef get_pairs_count(numbers, sum):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of unordered pairs in a list that sum to a target value.\n    This handles duplicate numbers correctly by counting combinations.\n    \"\"\"\n    freq = defaultdict(int)\n    for num in numbers:\n        freq[num] += 1\n\n    count = 0\n    for num in numbers:\n        # Decrement frequency of the current 'num' to avoid pairing it with itself twice,\n        # and to properly count for the num == complement case.\n        freq[num] -= 1 \n\n        complement = sum - num\n        if complement in freq and freq[complement] > 0:\n            count += freq[complement]\n            \n    return count"}
