{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "class TupleComparator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encapsulates the logic for comparing two tuples element-wise.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple):\n        if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n            raise ValueError(\"Tuples must have the same length.\")\n        self._tuple1 = tuple1\n        self._tuple2 = tuple2\n\n    def check_smaller(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if each element of tuple2 is smaller than its corresponding element in tuple1.\n        \"\"\"\n        for i in range(len(self._tuple1)):\n            if not isinstance(self._tuple1[i], (int, float)) or not isinstance(self._tuple2[i], (int, float)):\n                raise TypeError(\"Tuple elements must be numeric.\")\n            if self._tuple2[i] >= self._tuple1[i]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\ndef check_smaller(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if each element of tuple2 is smaller than its corresponding element in tuple1.\n    \"\"\"\n    comparator = TupleComparator(tuple1, tuple2)\n    return comparator.check_smaller()"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/583", "solution": "import math\nimport threading\n\n_catalan_cache = {0: 1}\n_cache_lock = threading.Lock()\n\ndef catalan_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Catalan number using the combinatorial formula with memoization.\n    Raises ValueError for negative inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Catalan numbers are not defined for negative n.\")\n\n    with _cache_lock:\n        if n in _catalan_cache:\n            return _catalan_cache[n]\n\n        # Compute using the formula C_n = (2n)! / ((n+1)! * n!)\n        # This is equivalent to C_n = (1/(n+1)) * C(2n, n)\n        # We can also compute it iteratively C_n = product( (n+k)/k for k from 2 to n)\n        # Or C_n = C_{n-1} * (4n-2) / (n+1)\n\n        # Using the direct combinatorial formula is most straightforward given no prior values\n        # C_n = math.factorial(2 * n) // (math.factorial(n + 1) * math.factorial(n))\n        \n        # A more efficient way to calculate C_n = C_{n-1} * (4n - 2) / (n + 1)\n        # but this requires iteration, for a direct non-iterative approach\n        # the formula (2n)! / ( (n+1)! * n! ) is good.\n        # Let's use the direct formula, but since we are memoizing, an iterative approach\n        # that builds on previous values is good too.\n\n        # For efficient calculation and leveraging memoization, we can compute iteratively\n        # or just compute directly if not in cache.\n        # Since we use a cache, the iterative formula C_n = C_{n-1} * (4n-2) / (n+1)\n        # is efficient for consecutive lookups. However, if n is large and not C_{n-1} is not in cache,\n        # it would result in many recursive calls.\n        # A direct calculation is safer for arbitrary n.\n\n        # C_n = (1 / (n + 1)) * (2n choose n)\n        # which means C_n = math.comb(2 * n, n) // (n + 1)\n        \n        result = math.comb(2 * n, n) // (n + 1)\n        _catalan_cache[n] = result\n        return result"}
