{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "import heapq\n\ndef larg_nnum(items, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list containing the n largest items from the input list.\n    Uses heapq.nlargest for efficient retrieval.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Convert to list to ensure it's iterable and consistent for len()\n    # and heapq.nlargest, especially if 'items' is an iterator.\n    data = list(items)\n\n    if n >= len(data):\n        return sorted(data, reverse=True) # Ensure order is descending if n >= len(data)\n\n    return heapq.nlargest(n, data)"}
